# Text files are LF in the repository and in every checkout, Windows included. Without this, GitHub's Windows runners check text out
# with CRLF (core.autocrlf is on there), which breaks every test that compares file bytes and every shell script that is run there.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The ignore pattern for the macOS "Icon\r" file needs its carriage return: this file is not converted.
.gitignore -text

# Never touched: binary files (git guesses most of them right; these are stated so that no guess can change a byte).
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp3 binary
*.sf2 binary
*.zip binary
*.jar binary
*.kar binary
*.karmp3 binary
*.mid binary
